mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# The Cozy Hook - Backend API\n\n## Purpose\n\nThe Cozy Hook backend canister stores the product catalogue, admin-editable homepage and store settings, and customer reviews for The Cozy Hook, a handmade crochet boutique. It exposes them through a small public API and an OQL query layer used by the Caffeine Data Intelligence agent.\n\n## Public methods\n\n### Products\n\n- `getProducts() : async [Product]` - query. Returns the full product catalogue.\n- `getProductById(id : Text) : async ?Product` - query. Returns one product, or `null` when no product has that id.\n- `getProductsByCategory(category : Text) : async [Product]` - query. Returns products whose `category` equals the argument.\n\n### Admin settings\n\n- `getAdminSettings() : async AdminSettings` - query. Returns the current admin-editable settings: hero title and tagline, featured and sold-out product ids, bundles, press entries, currently-crafting text, product timers, and WhatsApp subscribers.\n- `adminLogin(password : Text) : async Bool` - update. Returns `true` iff `password` equals the backend-stored admin password.\n- `updateHeroText(title : Text, tagline : Text) : async ()` - update. Overwrites the hero heading and tagline.\n- `setFeaturedProducts(ids : [Text]) : async ()` - update. Replaces the featured product id list.\n- `setSoldOutProducts(ids : [Text]) : async ()` - update. Replaces the sold-out product id list.\n- `setBundles(bundles : [Bundle]) : async ()` - update. Replaces the bundles list.\n- `setPressEntries(entries : [PressEntry]) : async ()` - update. Replaces the press entries list.\n- `setProductTimers(timers : [ProductTimer]) : async ()` - update. Replaces the product timers list.\n- `setCurrentlyCrafting(text : Text) : async ()` - update. Overwrites the currently-crafting text.\n- `setWhatsappSubscribers(subscribers : [WhatsappSubscriber]) : async ()` - update. Replaces the WhatsApp subscriber list.\n\n### Reviews\n\n- `addReview(productId : Text, rating : Nat, reviewText : Text, authorName : Text) : async Nat` - update. Appends a review and returns its new id.\n- `getReviewsByProduct(productId : Text) : async [Review]` - query. Returns the reviews for one product.\n- `getAllReviews() : async [Review]` - query. Returns every review.\n- `deleteReview(reviewId : Nat, adminPassword : Text) : async Bool` - update. Deletes a review; returns `false` when the password is wrong or the id does not exist.\n\n### Product images\n\n- `setProductImage(productId : Text, imageUrl : Text) : async ()` - update. Stores or replaces the image URL override for a product. This is a URL/path mapping only (for example `/assets/products/whale-plushie.jpg`); it does not upload file bytes.\n- `getProductImages() : async [ProductImage]` - query. Returns every stored `(productId, imageUrl)` pair.\n- `getProductImage(productId : Text) : async ?Text` - query. Returns the stored image URL for one product, or `null` when none is set.\n\n### OQL\n\n- `schema() : async Text` - query. Returns the OQL schema of the exposed entities as a JSON document.\n- `execute(qJson : Text) : async Result` - query. Runs an OQL query (JSON) over the exposed entities and returns a typed Candid result.\n\n### Documentation\n\n- `getApiDoc() : async Text` - query. Returns this document.\n\n## Authentication and authorization\n\nAdmin access is a shared password, not per-principal identity:\n\n- `adminLogin(password)` is the only authentication primitive. The stored password lives in `adminSettings.adminPassword` and is seeded by the migration chain. It returns `true` only for the correct password and never traps.\n- `deleteReview(reviewId, adminPassword)` checks the password inline and returns `false` (never traps) when it is wrong.\n- All other update methods (`updateHeroText`, `setFeaturedProducts`, `setSoldOutProducts`, `setBundles`, `setPressEntries`, `setProductTimers`, `setCurrentlyCrafting`, `setWhatsappSubscribers`) perform no server-side authorization check - any caller can invoke them. The frontend gates them behind a successful `adminLogin`, but that is client-side protection only. This is a static, free website with no backend auth service; the password is not true server-side security and should be replaced with real authentication before handling sensitive data.\n- No public method requires a signed (non-anonymous) caller; every method is callable by any principal, including anonymous callers.\n- This app does not use Internet Identity. Admin identity is the shared password, so there is no per-app principal derivation origin in use and no delegation to warn about.\n\n## Units and encodings\n\n- `price` is a `Nat` in whole Indian rupees.\n- `timestamp`, `endTimestamp`, and `subscribedAt` are `Int` nanoseconds since the Unix epoch (`Time.now()` in Motoko).\n- Product ids are `Text` slugs (for example `whale-plushie`).\n- `imagePath` is a site-relative path under `/assets/products/` (for example `/assets/products/whale-plushie.jpg`).\n- `rating` is a `Nat` (1-5 by convention; the backend does not validate the range).\n- `features` and `productIds` are arrays of `Text`.\n- Optional values: `getProductById` returns `?Product`; `null` means not found.\n- No public method returns variants; failures are expressed as `Bool` (`false`) or `null`.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\n- Every method completes in a single message. There are no long-running operations, background jobs, or state machines, so no polling is needed.\n- `addReview` returns the new review id synchronously; the review is visible to `getReviewsByProduct` and `getAllReviews` immediately after the call commits.\n\n## Mutation retry safety and idempotency\n\n- The list-replacing setters (`setFeaturedProducts`, `setSoldOutProducts`, `setBundles`, `setPressEntries`, `setProductTimers`, `setWhatsappSubscribers`) are idempotent: each call clears the list and writes the supplied array, so retrying with the same arguments converges to the same state.\n- `updateHeroText` and `setCurrentlyCrafting` overwrite a single value and are idempotent.\n- `deleteReview` is idempotent: deleting an already-deleted id returns `false` and changes nothing.\n- `adminLogin` is a pure check and changes no state.\n- `addReview` is not idempotent: every call appends a new review and increments the id counter. If a client retries after a timeout where the first call actually committed, a duplicate review is created. There is no deduplication key; callers should avoid blind retries.\n\n## Errors, traps, and limits\n\n- Wrong-password and not-found cases return `false` or `null`; they never trap.\n- No public method traps on ordinary invalid input. `addReview` stores the rating as given (no range check).\n- The OQL `execute` endpoint traps on malformed query text (the trap message starts with `OQL: invalid query`); treat it as a developer/agent surface, not user input.\n- The product catalogue is seeded in the migration chain and is part of the source export; admin edits to settings are runtime data stored in the canister and persist across browsers and devices.\n\n## Non-obvious gotchas\n\n- The admin update methods are ungated server-side (see Authentication). Any caller who can reach the canister can change hero text, featured products, bundles, and so on. Do not rely on the frontend password gate as security.\n- `getAdminSettings` returns the full settings record including `whatsappSubscribers`; treat it as admin data even though the query is unauthenticated.\n- Settings changes are immediately visible to the customer-facing queries (`getProducts`, `getAdminSettings`); there is no cache or publish step.\n- The OQL entities `product` and `review` are public; the remaining entities (`bundle`, `pressEntry`, `productTimer`, `whatsappSubscriber`, `featuredProduct`, `soldOutProduct`) are controller-only and readable by the Data Intelligence agent (which calls as the controller) but not by end users."
  };
};
